              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The first ever recorded 4 × 4 magic square, the Chautīsā Yantra, at Khajuraho, India"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.838,
            0.848,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chau̐ tīs means 34. Why do you think they called it the Chautīsā Yantra? Every row, column and diagonal in this magic square adds up to 34. Can you find other patterns of four numbers in the square that add up to 34?"
            }
          ]
